1.17.0: the scene-linear door - raw input, exposure, halation

.nef and .dng files open through a second door that decodes the sensor
data itself, dependency-free: a TIFF walker, lossless JPEG (T.81
process 14, predictors 1-7, tiles and strips), Nikon's Huffman scheme
with its linearization curve, DNG linearization tables, black and white
levels, the as-shot white balance, the color matrix (from the DNG, or a
per-model table for NEF) and a bilinear demosaic; LinearRaw (ProRAW)
comes through demosaic-free. Output is scene-linear with the sensor's
white at 1.0. --linear takes a 16-bit PNG or RGB TIFF as scene-linear
without a gamma decode (dcraw -4 -T, darktable linear).

The pipeline opens a scene-linear image one stop up, so the sensor's
white sits a stop above display white; halation runs on those real
highlights, then a scene shoulder (identity to 0.75, exponential
approach to 1.0) rolls the top stop in before the film transforms,
which are display-referred. --ev moves from there, on any input.
--halation 0..2 scales the camera's glow (PJ_HALATION_OFF in the API;
zeroed options keep the preset). Clipped sensor channels clip to
neutral white rather than going magenta through the white balance.

polajuice develop INPUT writes the straight print of a raw (no camera,
no film); inspect reports the clipped fraction and mean level. The page
accepts .nef/.dng, shows the engine's straight print as the original
(the browser cannot decode raw), and has Exposure and Halation sliders;
superjuice and super8ify (EV=, HALATION=) take the same knobs.

Backward compatibility: JPEG/PNG/PPM input renders byte-identically to
1.16.1 - checked across 35mm-negative, polaroid-600, super8 and bw-35
with silver grain and edge effects on - because exposure and the
shoulder only act on scene-linear images and halation at its default
is the preset's own.

Tests: five synthetic raws in tests/raw/ (uncompressed and lossless-
JPEG Bayer DNG, LinearRaw DNG, Nikon-compressed 14-bit NEF, 16-bit PNG
via --linear) of one scene, generated by tools/make_test_raws.py and
tracked; every decoder must reproduce the gray card, white patch, ramp
and (DNG) the color patches exactly, the two Bayer decoders agree to
the bit, and the raw render at --ev -1 matches the 8-bit render on the
gray card while its white patch sits under 1.0 and its halation spreads
further. Movie, wasm, page and DOM suites cover the knobs and the raw
door in the engine. NEF color matrices are from memory of dcraw and
flagged for verification in PRESET_SOURCES; real NEF/DNG files from
the D610, D3200 and the iPhone are still needed to validate the
decoders beyond the synthetic round trip.
